The RTL module `i2c_master` exposes an interface through which it interacts with other components. Specifically, it has the following interface signals [Source: rtl/i2c_master.sv, lines 7-10]:

```verilog
input clk, rst, start;
input [6:0] address;
input rd_wr;
input [7:0] din;
input stop;
output reg [7:0] dout;
inout SDA;
output SCL;
```

These signals include clock (`clk`), reset (`rst`), start condition (`start`), 7-bit address (`address`), read/write mode (`rd_wr`), data input register (`din`), stop condition (`stop`), data output register (`dout`), serial data line (`SDA`), and serial clock line (`SCL`).
